{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nSix rollout-created comments remain duplicated in live Jira and reachable `tickets` history after\nthe reconciler fixes stopped the echo loop. Closed prerequisite `irongray-unlucky-discus` proved\nthe causal pairs and rehearsed it. The operator authorized the quiet window; direct\nwriter evidence, not an elapsed wait, controls entry.\n\nThe older bridge-cache reclaim preserved the HEAD tree, an invalid oracle for intentional removal;\nsee `docs/comment-echo-reclaim-runbook.md:21`, `:68`, and `:269`. Preparation found about 254 MB\nlogical removal but only about 26 MB whole-clone savings, so footprint is not a threshold.\n\n## Approach\n\nUpdate from `origin/main` with enrichment drain disabled. Prove writers stopped, synchronize the\nstopped AWS MCP clone to live `origin/tickets`, then freeze its OID/ref census after stable reads.\nAny movement restarts artifact generation.\n\nRegenerate evidence in a new `0700` off-repo directory and full clone. Use\n`prepare_reclaim_backup.prepare` (`infra/scripts/prepare_reclaim_backup.py:292`),\n`comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.build_manifest` (`infra/scripts/comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py:746`),\nand `reclaim_comment_echo_history.rewrite` (`infra/scripts/reclaim_comment_echo_history.py:743`).\nReplay both tips, rehearse rollback/forward, and probe stale deployed writers before mutation.\n\nWith the reconciler disabled, use only `cleanup_comment_echo_jira.run`'s digest-bound journal\n(`infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py:478`). Delete `997143,997144,997145,997255,997256,997293`;\npreserve `963510,963511,963512,963788,963789,964272`. Prove convergence twice, publish\n`refs/heads/tickets` once with the exact frozen lease, replace every persistent clone, then restore\nwriters one runtime at a time.\n\nThe manifest uses causal identity, the exact lease rejects movement, and the epoch rejects stale\nunion. It retains prior binary-safe framing, full-ref restore, durable Jira journaling, clone\nreplacement, and post-read checks without a recurring gate.\n\n## Scope\n\n`file_impact_scope=none` is deliberate: repository files are read-only. Only the six Jira\nduplicates, manifest-listed echo material, final epoch, `origin/tickets`, and persistent clones\nchange; sensitive artifacts remain off-repo.\n\nSurvivors, non-target state, bridge bindings, retained bytes, and other refs are excluded.\nPre-DELETE failure abandons the candidate. Post-DELETE failure keeps writers stopped;\nrollback/compensation needs separate approval because Jira cannot restore IDs.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: run `git fetch origin` then `git merge --ff-only origin/main`; inspect all writer\n  states and reconciler refs. Require\n  AWS `git rev-parse HEAD`, local `git rev-parse tickets`, and\n  `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/tickets` to agree before freezing.\n- Fresh candidate: execute the three runbook builder scripts from the cited entry points. Require\n  exact manifest cardinality, replay/authorship/graph/bridge parity, differential-plan parity,\n  threshold-free measurements, and `git fsck --strict`.\n- Failure path: disposable stores prove drift refuses before mutation, crash/resume issues no\n  second DELETE, a moved ref rejects `--force-with-lease`, and deployed old-epoch runtimes refuse\n  both union paths.\n- Rollback rehearsal: restore `OLD_TIP` to a disposable remote using\n  `git push --force-with-lease=refs/heads/tickets:\"$NEW_TIP\" disposable \"$OLD_TIP\":refs/heads/tickets`,\n  reapply `NEW_TIP` with the inverse lease, then require ref census/replay/fsck parity.\n- Live checks: run the Jira helper GET-only, inspect its six-action digest, then run\n  `python infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py --repo \"$SOURCE\" --manifest \"$MANIFEST\" --artifact-dir \"$JIRA_ARTIFACTS\" --execute --confirm-manifest-digest \"$MANIFEST_DIGEST\"`.\n  Require fixed survivors plus unchanged non-targets. Two production-runtime reads must plan zero\n  comment/label/link actions, perform no write, keep bytes unchanged, and reproduce the pinned plan.\n- Publication: run only\n  `git push --force-with-lease=refs/heads/tickets:\"$OLD_TIP\" origin \"$NEW_TIP\":refs/heads/tickets`.\n  A fresh clone must pass replay/fsck and reject old ancestry before writers restart.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Every known ticket writer is quiescent; checked from live workflow, queue, process, container, review-bot, service, and reconciler-ref evidence. Record `writer-freeze-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=prod-writers; principal=operator; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — live runtime receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The stopped AWS MCP clone equals the final live tickets OID; checked by three `git rev-parse`/`git ls-remote` reads. Record `aws-sync-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=AWS-MCP; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — live OID receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The fresh source yields one independently restored bundle; checked by `git bundle verify \"$BUNDLE\"`. Record `backup-restore-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=isolated-clone; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — bundle receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The manifest names exactly six authorized deletions plus six fixed survivors; checked by the builder and `shasum -a 256 \"$MANIFEST\"`. Record `manifest-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=frozen-Git-Jira; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — manifest receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Candidate replay has only the manifest delta plus epoch; checked by the whole-store oracle and `git fsck --strict`. Record `candidate-parity-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=isolated-candidate; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — parity receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Every deployed old-epoch runtime refuses both stale-union paths; checked by refusal exits with unchanged refs. Record `epoch-refusal-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=deployed-images; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=simulation — refusal receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Disposable rollback reproduces `OLD_TIP`; checked by the exact-lease rehearsal plus `git fsck --strict`. Record `rollback-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=disposable-remote; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=simulation — rollback receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Live Jira retains exactly `963510,963511,963512,963788,963789,964272`; checked by `jira-after.json`. Record `jira-cleanup-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=Jira-production; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — journal receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Two post-delete candidate passes plan zero comment/label/link operations; checked by equal canonical plan digests. Record `convergence-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=prod-reconciler; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — dry-run receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `origin/tickets` equals `NEW_TIP` after one exact lease; checked by the push receipt plus fresh clone. Record `publication-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=authoritative-remote; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — publication receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Every persistent writer starts at the new epoch; checked by clone OID receipts. Record `clone-replacement-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=prod-writers; principal=operator; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — replacement receipt.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Staged writer restoration creates no replacement target body; checked after each first pass by Jira inventory plus tickets replay. Record `non-resurrection-<UTC>`.\n  provenance: environment=prod-stores; principal=operator; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — restoration receipt."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787776465306411001,"uuid":"6573fc6a-5b56-4d09-a6fa-0fa2a9914b08"}